Timestral Forecast Android sample

Model: Timestral-209M by Mistral AI (huggingface.co/mistralai/Timestral-209M, revision
9874d252ab0aae16f7f7c999f98f98d6ad7d8365). The weights are licensed under the Modified MIT License
(licenses/Timestral-209M-weights-Modified-MIT.txt; attribution notice: 2026 - Mistral AI). Its
condition 2 withholds every right under that license from a user whose company, or employer, had a
global consolidated monthly revenue above $20 million (or its equivalent in another currency) in
the preceding month, and it applies to the model and to any derivatives, modifications or combined
works based on it. The LiteRT graph files and host tables the app loads are converted from these
weights and are installed on the device, not kept in this source tree.

The forecast's host steps are Kotlin ports of the official inference code (github.com/mistralai/
timestral, commit a534bdbd244d64f3d9d743f46c7bf6fc330ed4ff, Apache License 2.0;
licenses/timestral-code-APACHE-2.0.txt): the causal scaler, the asinh normalization, the
denormalization with clamp_nonfinite, the advancing refine frame of _refine_block, the quantile
cap, the NaN check, symmetric averaging and non-negative clipping of TimestralForecaster.forecast,
and the attention mask and positions of the forecast's two token streams. Changes include one decoder
block of at most 32 patches (1,024 steps), a context of at most 8,192 steps, fixed graph shapes
with left padding, and the context and its negation computed as the two rows of one graph call.

The example series in app/src/main/assets/examples/ and the test vectors in
app/src/test/resources/vectors/ are synthetic, made by scripts/make_test_vectors.py.

Gradle wrapper files retain their upstream Apache License 2.0 headers.
